tmp_text "Only be hit by the quest weapons...I like how you make that plural, meaning more than one causelast time I saw, haunters only had one quest weapon which killedhaunters very easily...What else is getting changed on this mud since group parties arentallowed anymore...what, once a quest is done in the day, the questdoesnt reset until reboot...???Gumbo**Heh, you know real changes are never posted here, you find most of them whenyour code bugs out and you have to read the inherited files to see what thefuck happened...Meech**The quest was intended to have 2 quest eapons.  one for the real questand one that worked somewhat also.besides.  you can still hold the haunter and most players can takethe 3 hits that are needed to kill him with the quest weapon.With the weapon the quest is MEANT to be solved by a single person.There used to be a quest on here that did reset only over reboot.but I think it was removed/fixed. not sure.  but this one was forthe good of players I think. In other words it should not hurt them. ;)-Mangla**oki, we finished our language system ....what is it about:you will now be able to speak in more than one language. at this time,there are 2 languages in the game, common and nihonese. more will follow(e.g. every race will get his own language). this system is already usedby the players and encourage you to put it into monster too.this means: if you have a monster acutally \"saying\", \"telling\" or \"shouting\"something, you should use this system. functions are documented, justtype \"man lsay\", \"lshout\", \"ltell\" and \"lcatch_tell\". an example how itworks is in \"/players/patience/example/example_monst\". feel free to look atit and copy it over if you want. if you have any questions related tothis system, ask me. (if i ain't really busy, i will answer gladly. if ido not reponse at once, keep on trying asking me, i will response as soonas possible).i learned, that samurais are able to speak nihonese too. so please talkto me how to install this system to your guild. i will help,of course. i am happy if you use this and enrich your guild and wouldnot consider this as stealing of my code or ideas (as i would nothingconsider so)patience**The one thing I would like to see with the language system is that if youcan not speak the language then it should say something about a foreignlanguage or something, possibly even saying what the language is, insteadof having the player speak and get a bunch of crap like -Player says: jrtehb 9htupmfhyv.Considering that if this is suppose to be multi-cultured (that is, each racehas its own heritage and such), then everyone would have bits and pieces ofdifferent languages.  And though one wouldn't understand it, one would be ableto at least differentiate the language base, and therefore know that a certaintongue was such a language, instead of just ramblings.>>>>>Axlrose - ...<<<<<**about the scrap on your screen:it will be handled in the near future the following way:if you do not understand the language at all, you will get scrap asyou get now.if you do understand the language (and be it only a bit) you will getscrap with bits of information. the better you understand the languagethe more of the message will be not scrapped.example: a player says: Hello Tatsuo, i like your guild very much !no chance to understand: sdlkf sdlkfsl, d sdflk lkdsf ... (scrap)fully understandable:   Hello Tatsuo, i like your guild very much !partly understood:      Helko Tadsuo, i like yokr guils very muxh !that's why, you will get scrap. the reason, why you now get ONLY scrapis, that i have to finish the system. it is not that easy, i haveto think of a proper algorithm (herp offered help in doing one inthe parser). but this will change soon and then the \"partlyunderstand\" will make sense (and the scrap too)btw: it works on other muds and is very much appreciated there. so i amsure, it is a good thing in this mud too. also there will belanguages for all the races too and one extra for wizards (casting)hope, you now see my point of viewpat** Hi I was just asked to fix a bug by a player and don't have rights for that so bug is in room  /players/tamina/castle/rooms/alchemi  on line 109 where is command     p1 = CLO (\"/players/kasgaroth/poison/poison\"); which sounds reasonable but that directory doesn't exist any more   so please change it to right poison path.    Thanks & Bye  Silver the Silver**Found now out what happened.The poison path was moved to Krylls dir, since kryll is nowgm of the guild :)             The bug is fixed now  Thankx again                           Whisky**Please. There is a bug in pick_any_obj() in monster.c If you want to see where exactly, clone /players/goldsun/nottingham/monster/soldier.cand drop an object. Soldier cannot pick it up at first time !Be more careful next time, if you change functionsGoldsun.By the way, add_poison() fuctions make me some problems too,someone changed variables in headline and i had to fix some monsters:(**use /p/g/nottingham/monster/guard.c**Thanks for info      Looks fixed now :   Whisky**I can understand what yuou are saying about somequests such as 'haunter of the dark' but i cannotcomprehend as to why. To my understanding the questweapon to kill haunter would take as long as killinghim with a huge party - A player should not not be penalized for doing it that way if they wish - ittakes a lot more planning to complete a quest suchas haunter with a group more so than by a singular player.In addition to that, I cannot understand how certainwizards expect players to complete some of these newquests on there own that invole killing monsters thatcan and could very eaily kill them in a few hits. If the goal of quests has become promotion of singular completetion, then maybe you guys should re-examixesome of these quests that you have installed, becauseI can rememeber what it was like to do some of theharder quests as a player - like wol, haunter, vampire,and orb! these quests involve killing several monsters that on your own would take nearly two hours to complereack - complete one small aspect of a quest. just wanted togive you quest questioners something to think aboutbefore you go changing them in one player a quest area!Concerned!Apollo**This note pertains to all guild masters who intend tochange the login of players in there guild to thereguild rooms. I encountered a problem with Tatsuo'sbabrbarian guild this morning - the problem was that/players/tatsuo/guild/room.c was bugged and when youhave players login to that room they also become buggedand cannot go anywhere. I like the idea of logging intoguilds that  are hard to reach - however I do think youshould take a count of how many 'players' actuallylike this idea - and they choose to log on from thereguild you should create a backup code line that moves them to /room/church.c so that they can do what is neededto either play or informwho they have to! thank you and please check into whatI said earilir about bugged login rooms other than /room/church.cthat are used as login points.Apollo.wiz onwizACK**The original code was written for a single player to killthe haunter. Groups can go after the giants, or a singleplayer with a hold spell. The first person to do the questdid it alone. As for the new quests.  Yes they are just beingthrown out there, but such if the HM way. All gungho andlet the players debug it as they go along. Right now we arein a spiral that appears to need a crash landing the stop it.This is the war of guild powers. One GM changes code and then2-5 others think tht was unfair so change thiers to be \"tougher\"and so on and so forth. Want to worry about un fair to playerthen check out the legends system.  I am having appeals frommy guild NOT to put it in. They would rather have the funof having a tough fight than to run around with 1500 HPand 1200 SP. Takes the fun out of it.  Guild wars are thewhat I believe to relaly be the out of control factor.-Mangla**i do not disagree with new quests being added, I dohowever disagree as to wizard's methods of testing their respectice areas - especially quest areas. Anew quest should be gone over and finely tuned as tomake sure few if any bugs sneek through - ie. throughsyntax, coding mistakes, and generally too tough.There are more than enough players on here who seem to love to kill and the challenge that ensues. Why not ask them to test out the area/quest and therespective wizard snoops them. I think that manywizards are forgetting what is and what is not possible by a player on Holy Mission right now. Onegripe that I do have is that you say Haunter of theDark was meant for one player - that may be true,however it is also true that not many knew how tomake the secret quest weapon that killed him in10 hits. One reason for this is the fact that I canremember that as a player it was bugged for thelongest time and no one could fix it, so a logicalalternative to making it was to kill him in a largegroup. There appears to be so many monsters on thisgame that are almost untouchable by one player, butin a group they are decent monsters to kill. TakeHaunter, Dracula, Shao Kahn, Balor, and Kyoshi forexample ... each and everyone of those has a lotof HPS and for one player in todays standards couldnot even nick. So what do they do, they create parties to kill them. Then as a result quest info.starts, then cheating by players, etc etc. Ifwizards are set on making a quest singular in naturethen how about simply restricting the quest roomswith a code line that allows one person in it at a time. I can remember when a players biggest problemwas to find a way to gate other players into anarea and it seems like no matter how much wizardstry to prevent it, another wizard sneaks his owncoding idea of how to get around it in. And yes,therefore it is a repeating cycle that should stop.Will it stop? That is another question all by itself.We were given test characters for a reason and yetsome wizards test a monsters strength on how many'zaps' it takes to kill it. A player does not have'zap' and so it should not be tested by it. just some kind words to think about ...Apollo**we changed the wimpy, that you now can wimp during multi-attacks too.i moved the whole stuff from the heart-beat of the player/monster tothe attack(). this means that you now must be more carefulwhen overwriting or shadowing the attack().format of attack() is: varargs int attack( object weapon, int hand )weapon is the weapon, with which you hit and hand is the hand,which you use for the attackreturn-code is 0, when there is no fight anymore and 1 if there isstill a fight !the return-codes must be valid !!!!!!!!!!!so, if you have a monster which overwrites the attack() or if you shadow the attack(),please make sure that the returnvalues are correct.if you call attack() more than once in the function, take care of what youget back of it. abort at once when the return-value is 0. cos this means,that either the monster/player wimped or is dead.this is no drastic change to the lib, it has been the same way before.only a lot of you ignored that return-value.oki, that all for now folks.pat**HijaThe there is the infravision needed for the mage_guild.And later sure for other purposes too.....Its important that all rooms are /room/room therefore, unlessit can give light level bugs.         Please if you have some rooms not room/room ... recode them            Thankx in advance Whisky**changes in the combatsystem:1. there is now a list of ppl/npcs, the npc hunts. at the moment the npc   hunts up to 5 objects.2. players do not hunt any longer3. alt_attacker_ob is no longer valid ! it remains in the lib until all   files using it are recoded. i will post a list of mobs still using it4. new functions:   object *get_hunted()    returns an array with the hunted objects   void add_hunted( obj ) tell the monster that there is a new one to hunt   void present_hunted(obj) is s.b. of my hunted list in my env   void empty_hunted()   removes all hunted objects   these functions are only valid at npcspat**Just would like all to know that Matt gave me permission to make a questfor over level 20 characters. I have been coding it for a long time andwould be VERY angry if i were not allowed to intergrate it, I  am justmaking sure that everybody knows that I am making one so that no one willtell me that no more quests are allowed, also this quest is going to replace moonchild's area, if anybody is upset at this i am sorrythe reason for me doing this is that the draconians are not properly coded,airborne is supporting my-recodning of the area. Hope I do not inconvenienceanybody by my new area, and I hope it will be done soon,take it easy, Tanthalas**I believe the dracs give an orb that solves the orb questso be careful as to what you do with the area. it was made asan alterantive to doing it the long way even thoughthis is harder. as another question - what areasare you relacing???? surely not all of moonchilds areas - theyare a trade mark for this game from when it started!!!Apollo**Sorry about the confusion about the last message I wrote. My area is only going to replace the dark_forest area of moonchild's area, the area with the draconians. As for the orb, I am not sure what is up, since when I tried to do the orb quest, the draconian leader was not in operation, if anyone would like to make sure that I do not ruin this part of the quest, feel free to tell me how that part of the quest is accomplished, since the draconianleader is no longer in moonchild's area to my knowledge and if he is, he is coded to be invisible. Hope that answers your question, feel free to 